11. Competency: The Interplanetary Additions

The six domains from v0.1 are retained as an organising framework, but the candidate contribution is narrowed. The IMI ICQAP already covers cultural frameworks, self-awareness, multi-cultural perspectives, communication, preparation, and process management. The interplanetary additions are mandate-limit recognition under blackout, dispute classification for referral, intellectual integrity under strategic misinformation, and latency attribution. Each is assessed through an observable task, not a self-report instrument.

Competency Performance test Scored outcome
Mandate-limit recognition Scenario with a decision that exceeds mandate; participant must defer or refer Correct deferral/referral rate
Dispute classification Set of complex disputes; participant must classify and justify Classification accuracy against expert panel
Integrity under misinformation Scenario with one false factual claim; participant must identify and correct Detection and correction accuracy
Latency attribution Transcript with mixed unavoidable and deliberate delays; participant must attribute Attribution accuracy against ground truth

These instruments are proposed, not validated. Their reliability and predictive validity are objects of study, not assumptions.

