Appendix J: Adversarial Collaboration Plan

J.1 Purpose

The adversarial collaboration plan is a formal commitment to invite a sceptic to co-design the falsification condition and to have access to data and analysis before publication. The purpose is to ensure that the framework is tested against the strongest available challenge, not against a straw man.

J.2 Selection of Adversarial Collaborator

· Criteria: Published critique of the framework's approach, or expertise in a rival approach (e.g., sovereign liberation, rational choice institutionalism, critical theory).
· Selection: By the principal investigator, in consultation with the supervisory team.
· Independence: No prior co-authorship with the principal investigator; no funding relationship.
· Compensation: Honorarium or co-authorship, as agreed.

J.3 Role of Adversarial Collaborator

Stage Role
Design Co-design the falsification condition; review treatment operationalisation; identify confounds
Preregistration Sign the preregistration as a collaborator; may submit a dissenting note to be published alongside
Data collection Access to raw data; may conduct independent analysis
Analysis Review analysis plan; may propose alternative specifications
Publication Co-author if agreement; may publish dissenting note if disagreement

J.4 Dissent Procedure

If the adversarial collaborator disagrees with the interpretation of results:

1. The collaborator submits a written dissent (≤ 2,000 words) within 30 days of draft completion.
2. The dissent is published as an appendix to the main paper, or as a companion paper, at the collaborator's choice.
3. The main paper must acknowledge the dissent and respond to its substantive points.

